\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces (a) Wheat yield distributions by country (2003-2020). Germany has the highest average yield (7.35 t/ha) and the widest spread across its 251 NUTS3 regions. (b) Average wheat yield over time by country. The 2018 European drought is visible as a synchronised dip, with Germany experiencing the largest decline ($-7.3\%$ relative to other years).}}{9}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:yield_dist}{{3}{9}{(a) Wheat yield distributions by country (2003-2020). Germany has the highest average yield (7.35 t/ha) and the widest spread across its 251 NUTS3 regions. (b) Average wheat yield over time by country. The 2018 European drought is visible as a synchronised dip, with Germany experiencing the largest decline ($-7.3\%$ relative to other years)}{figure.3}{}}
